.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-suspend 1  "ngx-suspend " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-suspend \- Suspend a site: every request gets a 503 and a notice page (`ngx resume` brings it back as it was)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-suspend\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Suspend a site: every request gets a 503 and a notice page (`ngx resume` brings it back as it was)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
HTML page to show visitors (default: a short \\"temporarily unavailable\\" page)
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Note for yourself, shown by `ngx show` (never served to visitors)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would change without touching anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID (from `ngx ls`) or any of its domain names
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  ngx suspend 4
  ngx suspend shop.example.com \-\-page /srv/notices/suspended.html \-\-reason "invoice 2026\-11 unpaid"

The site\*(Aqs settings are kept; the certificate keeps renewing. Running it again updates the page or the reason.
